(RESERVE BANK OF INDIA) Tj
T*
(DEPARTMENT OF REGULATION, CENTRAL OFFICE, MUMBAI) Tj
T*
(RBI/2024-25/132 DOR.CRE.REC.54/21.04.172/2024-25) Tj
T*
(September 22, 2024) Tj
T*
(Scale Based Regulation \(SBR\) - Regulatory Framework for Non-Banking Financial Companies) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Categorization Layers: Under the Scale Based Regulation framework, NBFCs are categorized into four layers based on size,) Tj
T*
(activity, and perceived riskiness: Base Layer \(NBFC-BL\), Middle Layer \(NBFC-ML\), Upper Layer \(NBFC-UL\), and Top Layer \(NBFC-TL\).) Tj
T*
(2. Net Owned Fund \(NOF\) Requirement: The minimum Net Owned Fund requirement for NBFC-ICC \(Investment and Credit Companies\),) Tj
T*
(NBFC-MFI \(Micro Finance Institutions\), and NBFC-Factor is fixed at rupees ten crore \(INR 10,00,00,000\). Existing entities falling) Tj
T*
(short of this requirement must achieve the rupees ten crore threshold by March 31, 2027.) Tj
T*
(3. Middle Layer Threshold: Non-deposit taking NBFCs with asset size of rupees one thousand crore \(INR 1,000 crore\) and above,) Tj
T*
(and all deposit-taking NBFCs irrespective of asset size, are classified under the Middle Layer. Core Investment Companies \(CICs\)) Tj
T*
(and Infrastructure Finance Companies \(IFCs\) are also placed in the Middle Layer.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
9 0 obj
<< /Length 816 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(4. Core Banking Solution \(CBS\): NBFCs in the Middle Layer and Upper Layer having ten or more branches must mandatorily adopt) Tj
T*
(Core Banking Solution \(CBS\) software across all branches on or before September 30, 2025.) Tj
T*
(5. Ceiling on IPO Financing: The ceiling on financing for subscription to Initial Public Offerings \(IPOs\) is fixed at rupees one crore) Tj
T*
(\(INR 1,00,00,000\) per individual borrower. NBFCs are strictly prohibited from granting any credit facility exceeding this ceiling) Tj
T*
(for IPO subscriptions.) Tj
T*
(6. Capital Adequacy for NBFC-ML: NBFCs in the Middle Layer shall maintain a minimum Capital to Risk-weighted Assets Ratio \(CRAR\) of) Tj
T*
(15 percent on an ongoing basis, consisting of minimum Tier 1 capital of 10 percent.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
10 0 obj
<< /Length 863 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(7. NPA Classification Period: The overdue period for classification of loans as Non-Performing Assets \(NPAs\) across all categories) Tj
T*
(of NBFCs is harmonized to ninety calendar days \(90 days\). Upgradation of accounts classified as NPAs can only be done upon full payment) Tj
T*
(of entire arrears of interest and principal.) Tj
T*
(8. Chief Compliance Officer \(CCO\): NBFCs in the Middle Layer and Upper Layer shall appoint a Chief Compliance Officer to ensure independent) Tj
T*
(compliance oversight. The CCO shall have a minimum tenure of three years and cannot be removed without prior Board consultation.) Tj
T*
(9. Internal Audit Architecture: NBFCs in the Upper Layer and Middle Layer shall adopt Risk-Based Internal Audit \(RBIA\) frameworks,) Tj
T*
(reporting directly to the Audit Committee of the Board.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
11 0 obj
<< /Length 818 >>
stream
BT
/F1 10 Tf
50 720 Td
13 TL
(10. Mandatory Listing for Upper Layer: NBFCs identified and classified in the Upper Layer \(NBFC-UL\) must be mandatorily listed on) Tj
T*
(recognized stock exchanges within a maximum time frame of three years from the date of identification.) Tj
T*
(11. Disclosures in Annual Financial Statements: NBFC-UL entities shall disclose corporate governance scores, exposure to real estate,) Tj
T*
(capital market exposures, and ratings assigned by external credit rating agencies in notes to accounts.) Tj
T*
(12. Top Layer Classification: The Top Layer remains empty by default and shall only be populated if the Reserve Bank determines that) Tj
T*
(an Upper Layer NBFC poses extreme systemic risk.) Tj
T*
(Yours faithfully,) Tj
T*
(\(Manish Parashar\)) Tj
T*
(Chief General Manager) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
